trajectory.message:
## DramaFinder 1.1.6 — Usage Recipe

**No javadoc/sources jar exists in the repo** — everything below comes from decompiling the classes with `javap`. No `@ExtendWith` is needed: the base class already carries JUnit 5 lifecycle annotations that your subclass inherits.

### 1. Base class: `org.vaadin.addons.dramafinder.AbstractBasePlaywrightIT`
```java
public abstract class AbstractBasePlaywrightIT implements HasTestView {
    protected Page page;                       // ready to use in each test

    @BeforeAll static void setup();             // Playwright.create() + chromium.launch(headless=isHeadless())
    @AfterAll  static void cleanup();
    @BeforeEach void setupTest();                // page = browser.newPage(); page.navigate(getUrl()+getView());
                                                  // waits for Vaadin client to be idle; sets 4s nav / 15s default timeouts
    @AfterEach void cleanupTest();
    protected Page getPage(); protected Browser getBrowser(); protected Playwright getPlaywright();
}
```
`HasTestView`: `String getUrl();` (abstract — implement it) and `default String getView() { return ""; }`.

Headless is controlled by system property `headless` or env `HEADLESS` (defaults to headless=true if unset) — no browser download attempted, it just launches whatever Chromium Playwright finds, so it's fine in your offline sandbox.

### 2. Minimal test skeleton
```java
@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = SpringBootTest.WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT)
class MyViewIT extends AbstractBasePlaywrightIT {

    @LocalServerPort int port;

    @Override
    public String getUrl() { return "http://localhost:" + port + "/"; }
    // optional: @Override public String getView() { return "my-view"; }

    @Test
    void filtersGrid() {
        TextFieldElement.getByLabel(page, "Name").setValue("vir");
        MultiSelectComboBoxElement statusField = MultiSelectComboBoxElement.getByLabel(page, "Status");
        statusField.selectItems("ACTIVE", "CLOSED");

        GridElement grid = GridElement.get(page);
        grid.waitForGridToStopLoading();
        grid.assertRowCount(3);
        String cell = grid.findRow(0).get().getCell("Name").getTableCellLocator().textContent();

        String url = page.url();   // plain Playwright API — no wrapper needed
        assertTrue(url.contains("name=vir"));
        assertTrue(url.contains("status=ACTIVE,CLOSED"));
    }
}
```

### 3. Element access patterns
- Most field-like elements expose `static X getByLabel(Page|Locator, String)` (`TextFieldElement`, `ComboBoxElement`, `MultiSelectComboBoxElement`, `EmailFieldElement`, etc.) plus instance `setValue`/`getValue`/`assertValue` via the `HasValueElement` interface.
- `ButtonElement.getByText(page, "Save")` / `.getByLabel(...)`, then `.click()`.
- `GridElement.get(page)` or `.getById(page, "my-grid-id")`; then `findRow(i)`, `.getCell(colIndex|colHeaderText)`, `assertRowCount`, `assertCellContent`, `select(i)`, `waitForGridToStopLoading()`.
- `MultiSelectComboBoxElement`: `selectItem(s)`, `deselectItem(s)`, `getSelectedItems()`, `assertSelectedItems(...)`.
- Everything ultimately wraps a Playwright `Locator` (`VaadinElement.getLocator()`), so raw Playwright calls (`.click()`, `.textContent()`, `.fill()`) work too.

### 4. Reading the address bar
No dramafinder wrapper exists for the URL — use plain Playwright: `page.url()` (call after `waitForVaadinIdle()` or a grid/query settle if the URL updates asynchronously via History API).

